          "id": "leech",
          "gloss": "leech",
          "definition": "A bloodsucking creature used as an image of appetite that cannot be satisfied.",
          "evidence": [
            {
              "ref": "Pro.30.15",
              "role": "defining",
              "note": "The two daughters keep asking for more. The next verse names the grave, the barren womb, thirsty land and fire as things that never say ‘Enough’."
